{
  "slug": "kaizen",
  "name": "Kaizen",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Continuous improvement toolkit for Claude Code. Instead of dumping a dozen skills upfront, kaizen starts with a single skill — /kaizen:coach — that analyzes your actual workflow and suggests only what you need:\nthe right skills, hooks, rules, and a well-structured CLAUDE.md. Once your environment is healthy, /kaizen:code handles the full dev pipeline: diagnose → implement → verify → commit.",
  "longDescription": "Installs with `claude plugin install kaizen@claude-community` from `imadAttar/kaizen`.\n\nMost Claude Code plugins give you a dozen skills upfront. You enable them all, use two, and the rest just bloat your context.",
